# Presentation only. No collision, production, capacity or placement rules.
# Restart the game after editing. This file is packaged as assets/sprites/objects.catalog.
# Columns:
# Optional final column: independent shared decor profile (or -).
# Enclosed wall/roof columns select generic material families, shared across work objects.
# object-id mode floor-id wall-id roof-id sprite-id module-width module-depth height wall-thickness front-shade side-shade edge-light shadow-alpha outline
# Modes: ground (flat), enclosed (walls/optional roof), modules (repeated props),
# single (one centered prop). "-" means no sprite; primitive fallback remains.
# Sprite IDs resolve through assets/sprites/sprites.catalog (PNG dimensions/pivot).
# Module dimensions are tile spacing; supplied sprites retain their own size.
# Missing art uses generic depth blocks, NOT final artwork. Heights are visual only.
# Set shade/light/shadow values to 0 for art with baked lighting. Outline is 0/1.
# Last four columns: placeholder fill-RGB frame-RGB body-width-fraction body-depth-fraction.
# Supplying ANY art for an object disables ALL its fallback shapes/outlines.
# Proxy lighting/shadows also disappear: transparent sprite pixels stay clear.
# Define all desired sprite layers explicitly; '-' layers stay absent with art.
# Open-area modules are clipped to the viewport and omitted at overview zoom.
city_keep enclosed city_keep.floor wall.adobe roof.thatch - 3 5 .85 1 30 65 32 65 0 dbd6c2 524d3d .6 .45 decor.tribal
